Disables Jekyll/Liquid processing for the GitHub Pages site published from
this directory.

docs/ is a static archive of rendered talks (.html from Marp, .pdf, .png).
Nothing here is a Jekyll source. But Pages defaults to running Jekyll, which
expands Liquid tags in EVERY .md it finds -- including inside fenced code
blocks -- so a plan or spec containing `{{` fails the whole deployment:

  Liquid Exception: Liquid syntax error (line 691): Variable '{{ {body}' was
  not properly terminated ... in superpowers/plans/2026-07-25-json-configurable-modes.md

Three files under docs/superpowers/plans/ hit this, and any future one would
too. The presence of this file (contents irrelevant) makes Pages serve the
directory as-is.
